# 117 Belmont Circle

117 Belmont Circle, Uniontown PA 15401 is a three-storey house on the edge

of the Uniontown Country Club's fifth fairway that

[[wiki/people/fran-coldren|Frances Whyel Coldren]] occupied for at least

fifty-seven years, and it is the most causally dense address in this wiki.

Four separate things that shape Dan Frank's life are anchored to this single

lot: the family's return to Fayette County, the golf lineage he inherited

rather than chose, the fifty-year property-line adjacency to

[[wiki/people/annie-ulmer|Annie Ulmer's]] grandparents that both families

read as fate, and the paid caregiving job that ended in the night documented

at [[wiki/timeline/events/the-fall-of-fran]]. It is also, for eight months

in 2018 — five of them after Fran was dead — the address Dan gave out when

he wanted somebody to come to him.

## The documentary floor: 1961, from Miami Beach

Every account in the corpus rounds Fran's tenure to "more than fifty years."

The Ancestry GEDCOM does better than that, and what it shows is a return

rather than a settlement. Fran is recorded living in **Miami Beach in 1957

and 1958**, with Florida events logged in February 1957 and April 1959 — the

same window in which her first documented hole-in-one was struck at LaGorce

Country Club. The next residence the record gives her is **Belmont Circle,

Uniontown, about 1961**, sourced to a *Pittsburgh Post-Gazette* item of

September 3, 1961.

The hard date is a wedding. On **8 February 1961** her only child, Rebecca

Diane Van Voorhis, married George Dixon Shrum Jr., and the GEDCOM records

the place of the marriage not as a church but as **Belmont Circle,

Uniontown** — the house itself. Their daughter, born in Pittsburgh the

following year, was **Suzanne Whyel Shrum**: Dan's mother

([[wiki/people/suzanne-frank]]). The house therefore enters the family

record already performing the function it performed until the last night —

holding the family's ceremonies indoors — and it does so **fifty-seven years

and one month** before Fran left it.

