## The listing

The house was re-listed after Fran's death, and the realtor was Danny

Matthews — a family acquaintance through Suz and, three weeks before the

occupancy ended, the third party at the door. On **2019-07-11** he reported

that it had *"finally went pending,"* with an aside — *"second time's a

charm"* — implying an earlier attempt had fallen through somewhere in the

preceding fifteen months.

That Danny is the only person in the corpus present at both of this

property's endings is not a coincidence in the Bacharach sense; Uniontown is

small and he sells houses in it. It is, however, the reason the property's

two terminal events are recorded at all. Both are in his thread.

### The sale closed

It closed in **summer 2019** for **$250,000** — operator testimony, and the

only account of the closing that exists. The pending status Danny reported on

July 11 held; the "second time's a charm" listing was the one that completed.

